        <Container name="Hints">
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_shroud">
                <English>Click a screw to take it out. %1 left in the shroud.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_wires">
                <English>Pick a wire (%1 / %2 or click it), strip it, then read it: only the battery feed is live, and the meter finds the coil and the solenoid.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_twist">
                <English>The clip is on wire %1. Strip another wire and twist to join them, or press Twist again to take the clip off.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_crank">
                <English>Hold %1 to crank, and let go the moment it catches.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_steering">
                <English>Hold %1 to force the steering lock.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_help_running">
                <English>It runs.</English>
            </Key>
        </Container>
        <Container name="Messages">
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_shroudOff">
                <English>The shroud comes off. The ignition barrel and its loom are in front of you.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_sheathed">
                <English>Nothing to touch there: strip the sheath first.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_nothing">
                <English>Nothing happens. Neither of those is carrying anything.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_turnsOver">
                <English>It turns over and dies. That is the starter, not the ignition.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_dashLive">
                <English>The dash comes alive. Find the starter feed and crank it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_immobiliser">
                <English>The dash stays dead. Something is cutting the feed to the coil.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_short">
                <English>A flash and a bang.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_alarm">
                <English>The horn starts blaring.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_fuse">
                <English>A fuse goes, and the loom is dead for a moment. %1 of %2.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_fuseDead">
                <English>Nothing in the loom yet: wait for the fuse.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_fried">
                <English>The harness is finished. This one is going nowhere until it is replaced.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_grind">
                <English>The starter grinds against a running engine. Let it cool.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_sheared">
                <English>The steering lock shears.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_running">
                <English>It runs.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_cutAlarm">
                <English>That was the alarm feed. It cannot sound now.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_cutImmobiliser">
                <English>That was the immobiliser. The coil can be fed now.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_cutDecoy">
                <English>Cut, and nothing to show for it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_cutFeed">
                <English>That was one of the three that matter.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_picked">
                <English>%1 unlocked.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_pickedIgnition">
                <English>%1 unlocked. It will not start without its key: get in and hotwire it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_hotwired">
                <English>%1 hotwired. It runs until someone with a key locks it again.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_msg_ignition">
                <English>%1 will not start without its key.</English>
            </Key>
        </Container>
        <Container name="Settings">
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_settings_sub">
                <English>Vehicles</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_enabled">
                <English>Vehicle locks and hotwiring</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_enabled_desc">
                <English>Picking vehicle locks on the board, hotwiring and the ignition lock. Off leaves vehicles to ACE, or to TLB Keys when that is loaded.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_hotwire">
                <English>Hotwiring</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_hotwire_desc">
                <English>A driver without the key can hotwire the vehicle they are sitting in, on the hotwire board.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_ignitionLock">
                <English>Ignition lock</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_ignitionLock_desc">
                <English>A vehicle that was locked, or broken into, does not start until it is hotwired. Off: picking the lock is enough to drive it away, and there is nothing to hotwire.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_steering">
                <English>Steering lock</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_steering_desc">
                <English>The steering lock has to be forced before the engine is cranked.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_armoured">
                <English>Armour can be hotwired</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_armoured_desc">
                <English>Armour and aircraft can be hotwired, with an immobiliser to find and cut first. Off: they cannot be hotwired at all.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_alarm">
                <English>Alarm feed</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_alarm_desc">
                <English>Service and armoured looms carry an alarm feed that sounds the horn if it is shorted. It reads exactly like a lamp feed on the meter.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_tools">
                <English>Hotwiring needs</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_tools_desc">
                <English>What the player has to carry to hotwire: nothing, any lock pick kit, paperclip or toolkit, or a toolkit only.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_tools_none">
                <English>Nothing</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_tools_any">
                <English>Kit, paperclip or toolkit</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_tools_kit">
                <English>Toolkit</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_shorts">
                <English>Shorts allowed</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_shorts_desc">
                <English>Shorts a harness survives. The next one finishes it, and cutting one of the three wires that matter finishes it on its own.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_friedTime">
                <English>Replacement time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_friedTime_desc">
                <English>How long a finished harness takes to be replaced before anyone can work on that vehicle again. The replacement has new wires in a new order.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_actionTime">
                <English>Working time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_actionTime_desc">
                <English>How long one screw takes. Stripping, twisting, reading and cutting are fractions of it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_crankTime">
                <English>Cranking time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlbi_vehicle_set_crankTime_desc">
                <English>How long the engine turns over before it catches.</English>
            </Key>
        </Container>
